course: dictionary
lesson: 14651
title: Words that come before
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A precursor is something that came before a later thing and helped lead to it. The start of the word, pre-, means before, so a precursor comes first.
explain: «The abacus was a precursor of the calculator.» The abacus came first, and later the calculator was built to do similar counting. To check your meaning, swap in a simple phrase: «The abacus was something that came before the calculator.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: A precursor can also be a sign that something is coming. «Dark clouds can be a precursor to a storm.» The clouds come first and warn you that the storm may follow. Look at the words around the word to find which meaning fits.
fact: A precursor is a noun, and its plural is precursors.
fact: «Precursor» means something that came before a later thing and helped it develop.
fact: «Precursor» can also mean a sign or event that comes before something else, as in «a precursor to a storm».
fact: In science, a precursor is a substance that another substance is made from in a chemical reaction.
fact: Useful phrases include «a precursor of», «a precursor to» and «an early precursor».
exercise: «The early bicycle was a precursor of the bikes we ride today.» What is a precursor here? | A rider who is always late | A bike that is very fast | A bell fixed to the handlebars | *Something that came before and led to a later thing
exercise: «Grey clouds rolled in, a precursor to heavy rain.» What does precursor mean here? | *A sign that something is about to come | A cloud shaped like a cup | A rainbow after the storm | A raincoat for a windy day
exercise: Find and copy the one word that means something that came before a later thing and led to it. | *precursor | modern | computer | keyboard
test: «The wheel was an early precursor of the car.» What does early precursor suggest? | A wheel that is square | A car that was built last | *A first version that came before a later one | A car that never moves
test: «Scientists mixed a precursor chemical to make the medicine.» What is a precursor chemical in this sentence? | *A starting substance that is turned into another substance | A medicine that is already finished | A tool for measuring liquids | A chemical that never changes
exam: Which phrase means a sign that comes before a storm? | a calm, bright day | *a precursor to a storm | a stormy sea | a storm of questions
